    "statementMarkdown": "A linear form in $k$ variables is an expression of the form $P\\left(x_{1}, \\ldots, x_{k}\\right)=a_{1} x_{1}+\\ldots+a_{k} x_{k}$ with real constants $a_{1}, \\ldots, a_{k}$. Prove that there exist a positive integer $n$ and linear forms $P_{1}, \\ldots, P_{n}$ in 2017 variables such that the equation\n\n$$\nx_{1} \\cdot x_{2} \\cdot \\ldots \\cdot x_{2017}=P_{1}\\left(x_{1}, \\ldots, x_{2017}\\right)^{2017}+\\ldots+P_{n}\\left(x_{1}, \\ldots, x_{2017}\\right)^{2017}\n$$\n\nholds for all real numbers $x_{1}, \\ldots, x_{2017}$.\n",
