    "language": "en",
    "statementMarkdown": "Line $\\ell$ touches circle $S_{1}$ in the point $X$ and circle $S_{2}$ in the point $Y$. We draw a line $m$ which is parallel to $\\ell$ and intersects $S_{1}$ in a point $P$ and $S_{2}$ in a point $Q$. Prove that the ratio $X P / Y Q$ does not depend on the choice of $m$.\n",
